{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790450899686,"sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","part":{"id":"prt_0df309ada0016267a743gRLmVQ","messageID":"msg_0df30445200112cRoDi4WM3oaw","sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790450899686,"sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","part":{"id":"prt_0df309ade001aNF0NgFY66br00","messageID":"msg_0df30445200112cRoDi4WM3oaw","sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","type":"text","text":"Search engines are blocked. I'll try Blender-render verification after writing the shader. Actually, a simpler approach: render via Godot's `RenderingServer` viewport capture. But cleanest approach: write a small editor script that captures the screen after startup. Actually, the task explicitly recommends `--quit-after N --write-movie output.png`. Let me just write the shader first, then try that command and see what it produces.\n\nLet me write the shader now, in the well-known VHS/CRT godotshaders.com style (with mipmap linear filtering and LOD bias for blur):","time":{"start":1790450899678,"end":1790450899680},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"resp_eada5477b6e349f199c7236f68bcdfdb_msg"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790450899705,"sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"write_11_f158f7fc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/screen_effect/screen_effect.gdshader","content":"shader_type canvas_item;\nrender_mode unshaded, skip_vertex_transform;\n\nconst float curvature = 7.0;\nconst float vignette_multiplier = 2.0;\n\nuniform sampler2D screen_texture: hint_screen_texture, filter_linear_mipmap;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\t// Centered UVs in the range [-0.5, 0.5]\n\tvec2 centered_uv = SCREEN_UV * 2.0 - 1.0;\n\n\t// Warp UVs to simulate screen curvature\n\tvec2 uv_offset = centered_uv.yx / curvature;\n\tvec2 warped_uv = centered_uv + centered_uv * uv_offset * uv_offset;\n\n\t// Cutout mask: fade to black outside of the curved screen bounds\n\tvec3 cutoff = vec3(step(abs(warped_uv.x), 0.5) * step(abs(warped_uv.y), 0.5));\n\n\t// Scanlines\n\tvec3 scanlines = vec3(sin(2.0 * warped_uv.y * 100.0) * 0.1 + 0.9);\n\n\t// Vignette: darken at the edges of the curved screen\n\tvec3 vignette = vec3(length(pow(abs(warped_uv), vec2(4.0)) / 0.5));\n\n\tvec2 warped_screen_uv = (warped_uv + 1.0) / 2.0;\n\tvec3 screen_color = textureLod(screen_texture, warped_screen_uv, 0.25).rgb;\n\n\t// Small LOD bias to blur the screen slightly\n\tvec3 color = cutoff * scanlines * screen_color * (1.0 - vignette * vignette_multiplier);\n\n\tCOLOR = vec4(color, 1.0);\n}\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/screen_effect/screen_effect.gdshader","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/screen_effect/screen_effect.gdshader","time":{"start":1790450899684,"end":1790450899696}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_write_11_f158f7fc"}},"id":"prt_0df309ae1001jcUH7MOZcXIz6K","sessionID":"ses_f20d04a71ffeeOqE9s07NNam72","messageID":"msg_0df30445200112cRoDi4WM3oaw"}}
